 - Body copy in the app viewport should stay at or above 12px, and primary controls at or above 44px, including the desktop phone preview. Self-host `Noto Serif SC` via `@fontsource/noto-serif-sc` woff2 files so the offline PWA does not depend on Google Fonts.
 - The first release chapter is a complete five-day campaign with concurrent customers, face diagnosis, product choice, order ownership, rival interruption, daily incidents, persistent consequences, and multiple endings. Keep the full campaign playable end to end whenever content changes.
 - The mobile release is an installable portrait PWA. Real touch devices use the full viewport with safe-area padding and finger-sized controls; the desktop device frame remains a preview surface only.
-- The consultation is no longer a fixed-answer form. Its required interaction rhythm is observe → ask one meaningful question → trial → read the customer's reaction → close or revise. Wrong recommendations may be refused; returning to the floor preserves the active session and outside competitive pressure.
-- Floor characters communicate opportunity state through entry, waiting, rival approach, selection, and exit. They are not player-controlled walkers. The player remains embodied through first-person service gestures, the work badge, and direct control over attention, trial, order ownership, and resources.
+- The consultation is no longer a fixed-answer form. After observing two facial cues, the player can type what to say or tap a prompt; the customer answers in character via DeepSeek when the local proxy is running, otherwise a fallback line. The required rhythm remains observe → ask → trial → close. Wrong recommendations may be refused; returning to the floor preserves the active session and outside competitive pressure.
+- Floor characters communicate opportunity state through entry, waiting, rival approach, selection, and exit. They stand on the painted counter stage with walk cycles, name tags, and speech bubbles. Clicking anyone inspects current action, mood, and relationship in the dock; consultation starts only from the dock button. The floor clock can be paused or sped up. They are not player-controlled walkers. The player remains embodied through first-person service gestures, the work badge, and direct control over attention, trial, order ownership, and resources. Do not collapse the floor back into floating name pills or skip the inspect step.
 - Beauty products must use real raster product art. Do not regress product selection to CSS bottle drawings or text-only placeholders.
+- Replacement floor, portrait, consultation, and product art must follow `art/blender-export.md`. Export right-facing 384×512 walk cells and 853×1844 consultation plates with locked face-cue landmarks. Do not put Xu Yuan on the floor as a walker, and do not replace the PWA with a Godot or realtime 3D scene.
 - Core named staff have distinct portrait assets in `public/assets/game/staff-portraits/`: Xu Yuan, Lu Yao, Roman, Su Man, Tang Ke, and Fang Min. Do not collapse them back into shared staff sprites or text-only markers. Each customer's map marker must carry that customer's own consultation portrait as an identity badge; do not infer identity only from an age-based generic sprite.
 
 In ChatGPT Work Mode, run `sites-preview start "$PWD"`, open `http://terminal.local:4173/` in the cloud browser, and verify the rendered app and its primary interactions. Keep that preview open and tell the user to inspect it in the cloud browser; do not present the local URL as a user-facing chat link. In Codex Desktop, run the local server yourself, open the preview in the in-app browser, and provide the clickable local URL. Do not deploy to Sites unless the user explicitly asks to share, publish, or deploy. Do not give the user server-start instructions when you can run it.
